§ `2. gratification: each of the five paragraphs alone`

`thing a: money` MEANS `Gratification Facts` WITH
    `the thing is money or a gift, loan, fee, reward, commission, valuable security or other property or interest in property of any description, movable or immovable` IS TRUE
    `the thing is an office, employment or contract` IS FALSE
    `the thing is a payment, release, discharge or liquidation of a loan, obligation or other liability whatsoever, in whole or in part` IS FALSE
    `the thing is any other service, favour or advantage of any description whatsoever, including protection from a penalty or disability or from disciplinary or penal action, or the exercise or the forbearance from the exercise of a right or an official power or duty` IS FALSE
    `the thing is an offer, undertaking or promise of anything within the other four paragraphs` IS FALSE

