§ `29, 30, 31. abetment, attempt, conspiracy`

`inchoate abetment` MEANS `Inchoate Offence Facts` WITH
    `the accused abetted, within the meaning of the Penal Code 1871, the commission of an offence under this Act` IS TRUE
    `the accused abetted, within the meaning of the Penal Code 1871, the commission outside Singapore of an act, in relation to the affairs or business or on behalf of a principal residing in Singapore, which if committed in Singapore would be an offence under this Act` IS FALSE
    `the accused attempted to commit an offence punishable under this Act` IS FALSE
    `the accused was a party to a criminal conspiracy, within the meaning of the Penal Code 1871, to commit an offence under this Act` IS FALSE

`inchoate abetment abroad` MEANS `Inchoate Offence Facts` WITH
    `the accused abetted, within the meaning of the Penal Code 1871, the commission of an offence under this Act` IS FALSE
    `the accused abetted, within the meaning of the Penal Code 1871, the commission outside Singapore of an act, in relation to the affairs or business or on behalf of a principal residing in Singapore, which if committed in Singapore would be an offence under this Act` IS TRUE
    `the accused attempted to commit an offence punishable under this Act` IS FALSE
    `the accused was a party to a criminal conspiracy, within the meaning of the Penal Code 1871, to commit an offence under this Act` IS FALSE

`inchoate attempt` MEANS `Inchoate Offence Facts` WITH
    `the accused abetted, within the meaning of the Penal Code 1871, the commission of an offence under this Act` IS FALSE
    `the accused abetted, within the meaning of the Penal Code 1871, the commission outside Singapore of an act, in relation to the affairs or business or on behalf of a principal residing in Singapore, which if committed in Singapore would be an offence under this Act` IS FALSE
    `the accused attempted to commit an offence punishable under this Act` IS TRUE
    `the accused was a party to a criminal conspiracy, within the meaning of the Penal Code 1871, to commit an offence under this Act` IS FALSE

`inchoate conspiracy` MEANS `Inchoate Offence Facts` WITH
    `the accused abetted, within the meaning of the Penal Code 1871, the commission of an offence under this Act` IS FALSE
    `the accused abetted, within the meaning of the Penal Code 1871, the commission outside Singapore of an act, in relation to the affairs or business or on behalf of a principal residing in Singapore, which if committed in Singapore would be an offence under this Act` IS FALSE
    `the accused attempted to commit an offence punishable under this Act` IS FALSE
    `the accused was a party to a criminal conspiracy, within the meaning of the Penal Code 1871, to commit an offence under this Act` IS TRUE

`inchoate none` MEANS `Inchoate Offence Facts` WITH
    `the accused abetted, within the meaning of the Penal Code 1871, the commission of an offence under this Act` IS FALSE
    `the accused abetted, within the meaning of the Penal Code 1871, the commission outside Singapore of an act, in relation to the affairs or business or on behalf of a principal residing in Singapore, which if committed in Singapore would be an offence under this Act` IS FALSE
    `the accused attempted to commit an offence punishable under this Act` IS FALSE
    `the accused was a party to a criminal conspiracy, within the meaning of the Penal Code 1871, to commit an offence under this Act` IS FALSE

