§ `18(2) and 21(2). failing to disclose; failing to comply with the Public Prosecutor's notice`

`18(2) ordered and failed` MEANS `Investigation Offence Facts` WITH
    `an order of the Public Prosecutor under section 18(1) authorises the officer to investigate and to require disclosure or production` IS TRUE
    `the accused failed to disclose the information or to produce the accounts, documents or articles to the person so authorised` IS TRUE
    `a written notice of the Public Prosecutor under section 21(1) was sent to the accused in the course of an investigation or proceedings into an offence by a person in the service of the Government or of a department or of a public body` IS FALSE
    `the offence investigated is an offence under this Act or under sections 161 to 165 or 213 to 215 of the Penal Code 1871, or a conspiracy to commit, attempt to commit or abetment of one` IS FALSE
    `the accused wilfully neglected or failed to comply with the notice within the time specified in it` IS FALSE

